    "name": "Segway Ninebot Max G2",
    "badge": "Best Overall",
    "category": "Long-Range Commuter, 450 W, 551 Wh",
    "description": "The Segway Ninebot Max G2 is the scooter we would point most commuters toward first, because it pairs a big battery with the parts support of the largest brand in the category. Segway rates it at up to 43 miles and 22 mph, from a 450 W rear motor that peaks at 1,000 W and a 551 Wh battery. Independent testing by ERideHero measured about 30 miles in regular riding and around 21 miles ridden hard, which is still enough for most round-trip commutes. Best Buy lists it as tested and certified to UL 2272 by TUV Rheinland, and Academy lists UL 2271 battery certification. It carries an IPX5 water-resistance rating and supports riders up to 265 pounds. The trade-off is weight: at 53.5 pounds listed, this is a scooter to roll, not carry, so it suits riders with ground-floor storage or an elevator. Regional versions differ in speed, so confirm you are buying the US model.",
    "pros": [
      "Rated at up to 43 miles from a 551 Wh battery",
      "Listed as UL 2272 certified (Best Buy) and UL 2271 (Academy)",
      "IPX5 water-resistance rating",
      "450 W motor with 1,000 W peak, per Segway",
      "Large brand with established parts support"
